ovations happening.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.323
It's getting crazy.

00:00:04.323 --> 00:00:06.297
- Oh my goodness. How y'all do it?

00:00:06.297 --> 00:00:08.952
(audience cheers louder)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:08.952 --> 00:00:10.010
- So, so let's start with you.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.025
So you're from Arkansas, right?

00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:11.858
- [Symone] I am.

00:00:11.858 --> 00:00:14.040
- So what was it like growing
up, growing up in Arkansas?

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:14.873
- Oh, child. You know,

00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:15.805
you're from the south too, aren't you?

00:00:15.805 --> 00:00:16.800
- I'm from Texas.
- You from Texas.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:17.970
You was next door.
- Yep.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.230
- Okay, so you know how it was.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.610
It was hard. It was hot.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:21.443
- [Kelly] Hot.

00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:22.276
- It was humid.

00:00:22.276 --> 00:00:23.109
- It can get judgey.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:24.248
- Yeah, it can get judgey.

00:00:24.248 --> 00:00:25.110
- Especially if you're in a small town.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.082
- Yeah, but you know, I was a shy kid

00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:29.426
so I was very to myself and you know,

00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:31.650
we had the bullies and all that stuff.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.820
But, I discovered drag.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.653
- [Kelly] Yeah, people don't believe me

00:00:33.653 --> 00:00:34.860
that I was shy too.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.693
- Really?

00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:36.960
- So wait, now when do you discover drag?

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.950
When you discovered that,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.300
did it kind of bring
you out of your shell?

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.530
Because when I discovered music

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.120
that's where my personality came in.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.350
- Absolutely, absolutely.
- Yeah.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.522
- And my mom, so my mom
saw me for the first time

00:00:45.522 --> 00:00:46.957
when I perform and she was like,

00:00:46.957 --> 00:00:49.376
"Who was that? Where'd that come from?

00:00:49.376 --> 00:00:51.390
I didn't even know you could
talk some of the times,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.620
how could you get up there and do that?".

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.300
- [Kelly] I love that though.
- Yeah.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.250
- But speaking of growing
up, so let, let's see.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.510
Jim as a teen-
- Oh.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.343
- [Kelly] cause I love this photo.

00:00:58.343 --> 00:00:59.880
- Oh my.
- [Kelly] Yep, let's see this.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.617
- Get ready, get ready to swoon.

00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:03.857
(everybody laughs)
(audience claps)

00:01:03.857 --> 00:01:04.690
