fade out my sister's face.

00:01:06.872 --> 00:01:07.705
(everyone laughs)
- [Kelly] We didn't,

00:01:07.705 --> 00:01:08.538
we didn't get the OK.

00:01:08.538 --> 00:01:10.530
- [Jim Rash] Don't show her identity.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.090
No, she's not speaking.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.470
- [Kelly] I was, I was braces as well.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.700
- [Jim Rash] Look at that, beautiful.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.950
- So, what were you like back then?

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.763
- Incredible. Final answer.
(everyone laughs)

00:01:18.763 --> 00:01:22.410
Final answer.
- Final answer, anything.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:24.990
- Oh, I, you know, it's not a shock.

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:26.070
Totally, drama club.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:27.480
Totally did all the, the the

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.111
questionable high school plays, you know,

00:01:29.111 --> 00:01:31.500
"Flowers for Algernon".
- Yes.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:32.857
- Cause every high schooler wants to see

00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:34.895
"Flowers for Algernon".
(everyone laughs)

00:01:34.895 --> 00:01:35.830
- [Kelly] Oh my God. I love it.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.830
- I was like the dad of Charlie,

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.480
if you know "Flowers for Algernon",

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.820
and I, you know, I grew
up in North Carolina

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.411
and so my version of New
York was like, you know,

00:01:44.411 --> 00:01:46.243
the mom's name is Rose, like,

00:01:46.243 --> 00:01:47.280
(speaks with New York accent) "Rose,

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.627
What about Charlie, Rose?"

00:01:49.627 --> 00:01:51.360
(everyone laughs)
"I'm worried about Charlie."

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.860
That's what it sounds like in my head.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:53.693
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:01:53.693 --> 00:01:54.540
We would've been friends (laughing).

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.680
- Yeah, right?

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.439
